# C01 primary Maven bootstrap data

This source-only proposal acquires only Help 3.5.1 and Dependency 3.11.0 primary JARs, POMs, sources JARs and their six official SHA-1 sidecars. Exact literal URLs, byte counts and actual checksum values are in proposal.json; metadata-readback.json preserves the official HEAD/checksum observations. Authoring fetched text listings, HEAD headers and bounded ASCII checksums only, never binary bodies, and executed no Maven/Java/plugin code or tests. The web reader could not fetch the repository; direct metadata-only HTTPS readback succeeded without redirects.

These primary files publish SHA-1 sidecars. The job verifies the pinned SHA-256/length of each actual sidecar and its declared SHA-1, then records strong SHA-256 for each acquired artifact. This is not independent signature/authenticity verification or complete source/binary correspondence. No SHA-512 values are invented. Future plugin execution requires its separate source, parent/plugin/dependency closure and actual invocation admission.

Root must review sources and freeze a clean allowlisted Python -I -B entry, existing compiler-lock descriptor, fresh Samsung/headroom/output scope, exact two-CPU/4-GiB-high/6-GiB-max/zero-swap/128-task cgroup and verified owned cleanup. The source requires those actual cgroup values; it creates no child process. Its phase limit is 600 seconds, with 60-second signal deadlines and 15-second socket timeouts per request; root supplies the independent whole-job bound. No proxy, credential, Maven settings, namespace, install or service change is needed. All redirects refuse.

Six primary files total 576,097 bytes; sidecars add 240. The 576,349-byte entity cap permits the bounded one-byte EOF probe on twelve bodies and does not claim TLS/wire or OS filesystem quota enforcement. Outputs have a 64-MiB logical admission bound. ZIP inventory admits at most 4,096 entries, 8 MiB per declared entry and 64 MiB aggregate uncompressed size; selected XML reads cap at 2 MiB. No extractall or path-based archive extraction occurs. Only fixed plugin.xml and optional embedded POM bytes are copied to fixed basenames. Complete raw descriptors and archives remain available alongside explicitly partial summaries; source JARs are inventoried rather than comprehensively reviewed.

The dedicated HTTPS/ZIP code counts as new implementation. The earlier distribution helper has different hosts, redirect and TAR semantics and is left unchanged. Input hashes, raw response headers from a safe allowlist, exact sizes/digests, partial files and failures are retained. No recursive dependency/parent/BOM fetch, Maven/Java/npm invocation, effective-pom/go-offline, plugin/class loading, native application, database, server or build belongs to this job. Parent C01, full dependency closure, native/UI and parity acceptance remain OPEN.

Mocked controls require an existing admitted Samsung SYSON_C01_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_TMP directory and SYSON_C01_BOOTSTRAP_SOURCE_SHA256 matching the reviewed runner. They perform no network request or acquired-code execution. Root owns actual normal/optimized control execution and acquisition after independent review. Reproduction needs a freshly reviewed output/launcher scope; this fixed job is not a generic downloader or build launcher. Maven's descriptor reference is https://maven.apache.org/ref/3.10.0/maven-plugin-api/plugin.html; primary repository URLs are pinned individually in proposal.json.
